TITLE:: Seq
SUMMARY:: The Sequencer for the front Document.
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events
RELATED:: Classes/Document, Classes/Sequencer

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::Seq:: is the shortcut for the LINK::Classes/Sequencer:: bound to LINK::Classes/Document#*current::. CODE::Seq():: calls LINK::Classes/Sequencer#*new:: with that document. The same document returns the same sequencer. Each call resolves the front document again.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Returns the LINK::Classes/Sequencer:: for LINK::Classes/Document#*current::. Throws if there is no front document.

ARGUMENT:: devMode
When CODE::true::, a sequencer created by this call stores dev mode. A sequencer that already exists for the document is returned as it is, and this value is ignored.

RETURNS::
The LINK::Classes/Sequencer:: for the front document.

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
Seq().addMidiSequence(\arp, \jx03, Pbind(
	\midinote, Pseq([51, 63, 70, 82]),
	\amp, 1,
	\dur, 0.25,
	\legato, 0.5
));
Seq().showGui;
::
